Subject: [PATCH v2] Cheap row-count-only instrumentation for EXPLAIN ANALYZE
 (wrapper variant)

When EXPLAIN ANALYZE runs with TIMING OFF and BUFFERS OFF (and no WAL
usage), the only per-node statistic needed is the row count.  Use a
lightweight ExecProcNode wrapper, ExecProcNodeInstrRows(), for such
nodes instead of the full ExecProcNodeInstr().

The flag, the "running" state and the counter are packed into a single
uint64 in PlanState (instr_rows), located next to the ExecProcNode
pointer, so the wrapper needs one load and one store per tuple.  The
packed counter is folded into the node's NodeInstrumentation by the new
ExecInstrEndLoop(), which replaces the existing InstrEndLoop() calls on
plan nodes.  Uninstrumented execution is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UovmohnnszTFF6bbcaFDhU
